WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.380
Selective cross-model collaboration lifts frontier model accuracy from 23.1% to 28.1% on hard reasoning, while using fewer tokens than full collaboration. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 183. Comed introduces a post-anchor controller that accepts confident answers from a single model. It probes peers only on ambiguous cases and escalates to collaboration when rescue value exceeds harm.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:34.480
The method decomposes performance into rescued errors versus collaboration-induced harms.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.840
Selective escalation improves results in all 16 open-weight settings tested.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:46.420
On MedQA, the approach adds up to 10.7% points while invoking fewer models and decoding

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:52.120
fewer tokens than dense collaboration. The controller relies on anchor self-consistency,

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:56.020
router margin, and a lightweight peer probe to make the decision.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.100
5.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:02.600
Open Weight Models were tested on generating kinship terms in Hindi, Tamil and Korean.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:11.360
GPT OSS 120B selected the correct term in 90.67% of valid cells, yet produced an accepted

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.100
term in only 36.00% of the same cells.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:24.720
Lama 3.370B showed 77.92% selection accuracy versus 24.24% generation accuracy.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:35.400
Accuracy on explicitly specified L3 prompts ranged from 72.29% for GLM 5.1% to 24.24% for

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:41.820
Lama 3.370B. A sentence-level data set of German federal constitutional court decisions

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:46.240
was annotated for seven interpretive canons in the Lerence Savignee tradition.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:52.280
Four LLMs from three families were evaluated under expert written prompts and genetic

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.820
Pareto optimize prompts.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:02:00.780
Mean F1 across the seven binary subtasks ranged between 70.4 and 79.2.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:06.120
Grammatical interpretation proved easiest to identify, while systematic interpretation

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:06.900
proved hardest.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:12.940
Lego combines an expert annotated civil code graph with greedy normative coverage retrieval

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:16.320
and a structured provision fact conclusion reasoning format.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:24.560
With a QN38B backbone, the system reached 40.53% exact match accuracy on law-exam QA

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:24.920
civil.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:31.180
It outperformed evaluated RAG and COT baselines, and matched larger models while remaining

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:33.180
robust on multi-hop questions.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:38.900
Ablation studies confirmed complementary contributions from both the graph RAG and COT

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:39.300
modules.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:45.680
The framework uses LLMs to measure repeated observable behaviors, then trains a classifier

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.700
on those behaviors for construct-level labels.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:58.260
On the talk moves data set, the best configuration achieved 0.673 macro F1 and 0.688 CoinsCAPA.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.440
The approach proved competitive with direct prompting while providing mechanistic insight

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:04.580
into label decisions.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:08.780
Two open tools for operationalizing the framework were released.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:15.580
UniData agent separates ontology acquisition from online execution using expert authored

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:17.640
business skills and constrained generation.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.420
Ontology construction for 27 enterprise tables

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:23.120
took hours instead of a week.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:26.320
Report generation dropped from several working days

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:26.880
to minutes.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:31.960
Strict accuracy on real business questions reached 95.0%

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:35.040
versus 72.5% for document rag.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:38.660
The system has already been deployed inside an enterprise.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.420
Locker uses hidden state trajectories

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:44.100
to detect early lock-in on incorrect answers

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:49.860
during iterative denoising. Across two diffusion models and three mathematical reasoning benchmarks,

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:55.940
it delivered absolute accuracy gains of 2.21 to 5.37 percentage points.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:03.480
Repair rates ranged from 22% to 41%. Hidden trajectories outperformed surface signals for both

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:09.780
detection and repair selection. PTTS replaces independent sampling with a planner that generates

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:14.400
distinct solution outlines for each branch before an executor completes them.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:21.500
PTS-ZS improved Passat 64 by up to 6.7 points over repeated sampling.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:28.560
PTS-RL raised the gain to 13.4 points across five mathematical reasoning benchmarks

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:35.740
with QN3.1.7B and 4B models. The method requires no changes to the underlying

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:45.540
executioner models. ISAC contains 527 million English Reddit posts spanning 2007 to 2023 and filtered

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:53.160
for six social group distinctions. A human-audited pipeline kept irrelevant content below 10%. Each

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:59.900
post carries region estimates plus validated labels for moralization, sentiment, emotion, and linguistic

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:07.380
generalization. The Corpus is accessible via website, SQL Playground, Python Package, and Hugging Face.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:15.880
Replacing DCUF Evidence with Unif EE Evidence raised strict score by 9.61% points on Feverus,

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:23.800
while answer accuracy rose only 1.96 points. The Evidence only contribution accounted for 7.92

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.640
to 9.08 points when answers were held fixed.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:32.620
Increasing context from 256 to 2048 tokens,

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:38.040
raised the fixed answer evidence gained by 3.10 to 3.84 points

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:39.320
for 2.8B models.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:43.140
UGT phone provides the first G2P benchmark

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:47.060
for user-generated text in English, Vietnamese, and Korean.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.980
Existing models showed canonical to non-canonical gaps,

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:58.700
reaching 66.8 PER points. A compositional approach using canonical form lookup and stage decoding

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:08.180
reduced non-canonical errors across by T5 and Quinn 2.5 0.5 B backbones. The 0.5 B model performed

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:15.160
competitively with larger few-shot frontier LLMs. The task supplied natural language definitions for

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:20.060
74 previously unseen specific genres in a zero-shot setting.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:26.060
Thica ranked first with 0.7352 hierarchical macro-F1.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:33.100
Huang Fong followed at 0.7169 and Nama at 0.7013.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:39.280
Broad genre recognition was strong, while fine-grained classification showed a substantial gap

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:40.800
under linguistic variation.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:46.820
Recurrent language models keep applying the same blocks across depth, yet most teams still

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:49.280
recompute full attention at every step.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:54.560
Attention support and distributions actually stabilize well before hidden states finish

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.100
refining, so you pop the hood on wise.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:03.600
Wise therefore runs unrestricted global attention only in the early recurrent steps to discover

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:04.860
a sparse working set.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:10.100
It then reuses that block structured support for the remaining steps while still allowing

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:15.840
dynamic within support attention. The approach preserves full attention quality through 2000

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:21.900
context with measurable loss only at 4000. An optimized sparse implementation delivers

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:29.900
up to 1.76 times the attention speed up at 4000 and 1.36 times speed up across a full 32-step

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:35.860
trajectory. Teams facing longer current traces should adopt working set reuse once context

00:07:35.860 --> 00:07:42.340
exceeds roughly 1,000 tokens. Test ComEd-style selective escalation on medical or scientific

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:47.780
queries using your current router plus a lightweight peer probe to see token savings firsthand.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:54.940
Run the UGT-FON compositional G2P approach on sample user-generated text in English or Vietnamese

00:07:55.360 --> 00:08:02.040
to measure the non-canonical error reduction. Explore the ISAC Corpus SQL Playground or Hugging

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:05.200
face release if you analyze social group discourse at scale.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:11.900
More results from the Natty 2026 multi-dialectal Arabic speech tasks are expected in the coming

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:12.320
weeks.

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:18.100
Additional papers on test-time scaling and hidden state trajectory repair are likely in

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.680
the next ARC-IVZ cycles.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:26.520
Further enterprise ontology agent deployments may surface as uni-data agent-style systems move

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:27.680
beyond pilot use.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:33.760
Before we go, a fresh round of test-time scaling results is already circulating in preprint

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.360
form and should land publicly within days.

